    "top_frame": "Shutout at home doesn't move the needle when the division is 27 games away.",
    "what_this_means": "Rafael Devers drove in three runs and the bullpen locked down Cincinnati for 6.1 innings, but a 5-0 win in August when you're 53-78 is a fact, not a statement. The early momentum was real. Two runs in the first, three in the second, and the game decided before the middle innings arrived. Whisenhunt exited after 2.2, and the back end delivered exactly what it needed to: Foley struck out three in 1.1 scoreless, Walker pitched two clean, and three more arms kept the Reds off the board. This is what execution looks like when nothing goes wrong. The problem is nothing that happened tonight changes the math they face tomorrow.",
